            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pūniō, pūnīre — \"to punish\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Magister discipulōs pigrōs pūniēbat. The teacher used to punish lazy pupils."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pūniō, pūnīre, pūnīvī, pūnītum, old form poeniō. From poena (taught). English punish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pūniō is built on poena, \"penalty\" (EtymDB), itself a loan from Greek poinē, \"blood-money\". English punish comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
