          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exsilium is built on exsul, \"an exiled person\" (EtymDB), which Lewis & Short connect either with solum, \"soil\", or with a root meaning \"to go\"; the origin is not settled. English exile comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
